Analysis is the detailed study of something by breaking it down into smaller parts to understand how it works or what it means.
Core Steps in Analysis
• Breakdown: Separate a complex topic, data set, or substance into individual components.
• Examination: Look closely at each part to see its function, features, or cause.
• Connection: Find relationships between the parts to see how they create the overall whole
Common Types of Analysis
• Data Analysis: Reviewing numbers or facts to find trends and answer questions.
• Chemical Analysis: Testing a physical substance to find out what elements it contains.
• Textual Analysis: Examining a poem, book, or article to understand its themes and language.
• Financial Analysis: Studying market data or business costs to guide decisions.
